Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:27:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Mass-consistent momentum advection at bottom-cell thickness
 jumps

With partial bottom cells, at u- and v-faces where the wet thickness of neighbouring
bottom cells changes, vector-invariant momentum advection is replaced by the flux form
(with the scheme's kinetic-energy-gradient scheme and the flux form's curvature terms).
Removes bottom jets and spurious mixing in thin partial cells next to thick ones.

